dsv41 patch 0041 (19.10.2026): choose the DSpark verify depths of all requests of a step together.
0010 picks each request's depth against the single-stream cost table, as if it paid a step's base cost alone. Here a step's
cost is one table of total live rows (TensorFold's multi-stream _choose_k prices a stream's rows next to the others' rows),
and the step maximizes (sum of expected tokens) / cost(sum of live rows). Exact solution: survivals fall with the position,
so the best m extra rows are the m largest survivals (prefix-closed per request); about 12 small device ops, no host sync.
With one request this is exactly 0010's "conf". Options: "cal=1" (per-position EMA of accepted / predicted, separately for
greedy and sampled requests: at T > 0 a greedy draft is accepted with the target's probability of it, so the confidence
head overestimates), "ctx=L:ms,..." (context cost per request), and a window cap for dynamic speculation
(num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size). Policy strings (env VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_POLICY or the live depth file):
"confb:<ms by depth>", "confr:<ms by total rows>"; "conf:<ms>" stays the default. Without new switches the image behaves
exactly as before.
Measured (19.10., GB10, 2000 MHz, T = 1, 1 / 3 / 4 streams, 4 interleaved runs per cell): confb against conf +-0.2 %
at 1 stream, prose 3 / 4 streams -1.9 / -2.3 %, code -1.9 / -3.0 %; confb + cal=1 -0.5 ... -5.4 %. conf stays the
default (README, "Tried, and not tried").

